Terms of the public site
------------------------
The public site (https://hotel-curator.fly.dev until it moves to its own
domain) is a free, non-commercial demo, published before the data licence
below has had a legal review. This project is not affiliated with or
endorsed by Booking.com or TripAdvisor. To request a correction or the
removal of a review excerpt, open an issue at
https://github.com/amit-badave-04/hotel-curator/issues.

Data sources
------------
1. Booking.com "515K Hotel Reviews Data in Europe"
   Original: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/jiashenliu/515k-hotel-reviews-data-in-europe
   Copy used by the pipeline: GitHub raghavendranhp/Dynamic-Hotel-Recommendation-System-Using-NLP
   at commit 903600f2ed2dbd761f2f435564c7e630f79e74b7, pinned by SHA-256.
   Licence: CC0 1.0, as declared by the Kaggle uploader. The uploader also
   states that the content was originally owned by Booking.com. This could not
   be confirmed first-hand from the build environment.
   Used for: training, evaluation, and display of short review excerpts.
   The raw data are not redistributed in this repository. Derived files that
   are committed (annotation samples, label files, the demo dataset) contain
   short review excerpts.
   Obtain a legal review before any commercial use.

2. Evaluation-only source (never committed, never used for training):
   TripAdvisor Annotated (Marcheggiani et al.), fetched by pinned hash,
   used only to measure annotation agreement. Licence not verified.

3. The archived v1 model (artifacts/models/v1-roberta-base, kept only to
   compare v2 with it, never served) was trained on Kaggle
   andrewmvd/trip-advisor-hotel-reviews with machine-made labels. That
   dataset's licence is not recorded here and could not be checked from
   the build environment.

Model
-----
The served model, roberta-base-ft-train2, is roberta-base (Liu et al.,
2019), fine-tuned on 13,845 review parts from source 1, labelled by a
language model following the project's guideline
(docs/labeling/GUIDELINES.md). The base model's licence is recorded as MIT,
as its authors published it (the fairseq release); it was not re-verified
from the build environment. The fine-tuned weights inherit the data's
licence uncertainty and come with no licence of their own: they are stored
in this repository through Git LFS and served only in the non-commercial
demo above. Model card:
artifacts/models/roberta-base-ft-train2/MODEL_CARD.md.

Third-party software
--------------------
The web app bundles open-source packages (MIT, ISC, BSD-3-Clause and
Apache-2.0 licences), and its build adds code from Tailwind CSS, Vite and
Rolldown (MIT; Rolldown's helpers derive from esbuild and Rollup, also
MIT). Their licence texts are in
web/public/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, served at /THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.
The API documentation page uses Swagger UI (Apache-2.0); its licence and
notice ship with it in src/hotel_curator/api/static/swagger-ui/ and are
served at /api/docs-assets/LICENSE and /api/docs-assets/NOTICE.
